WEBVTT

00:00:01.952 --> 00:00:03.984
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:04.878
Sammy!

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:07.588
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:07.611 --> 00:00:08.174
Go!

00:00:11.893 --> 00:00:13.101
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:15.186
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:19.021 --> 00:00:22.423
This is dad's book. I think dad
wants us to pick up where he left off.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.376
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:27.019
Family business. Do you think
Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:27.034 --> 00:00:28.145
I can't do this alone.

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:29.663
I'm driving.

00:01:02.047 --> 00:01:03.916
Man, these are some phat houses, huh?

00:01:04.292 --> 00:01:05.423
I'd like to live here.

00:01:05.761 --> 00:01:06.099
Yeah.

00:01:06.662 --> 00:01:08.208
Too bad you can't afford it.

00:01:09.162 --> 00:01:10.337
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:11.012 --> 00:01:13.350
This neighborhood will be
damn expensive when it's done.

00:01:38.128 --> 00:01:39.399
This place is perfect...

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:40.403
Ow!

00:01:41.597 --> 00:01:42.783
...Except for the mosquitoes.

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:47.600
Aah!

00:01:48.764 --> 00:01:49.244
Dustin?

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:51.683
Help me, I'm trapped!

00:01:52.635 --> 00:01:53.916
I broke my ankle.

00:01:55.469 --> 00:01:56.491
I'll get a rope!

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:00.037
Oh, damn.

00:02:17.209 --> 00:02:18.164
Oh god!

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.249
Travis, help!

00:02:30.411 --> 00:02:31.210
Hang on!

00:02:41.535 --> 00:02:43.013
Travis, help!

00:02:43.473 --> 00:02:45.275
Aah! Aaah!

00:02:45.301 --> 00:02:47.025
It's okay, Dustin. It's okay.

00:02:50.464 --> 00:02:51.017
Dustin?

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.407
Dustin, I'm here.

00:02:55.682 --> 00:02:56.445
Oh, god.

00:03:04.368 --> 00:03:06.103
<i>I got something to say.</i>

00:03:22.721 --> 00:03:23.436
<i>Ow!</i>

00:03:25.952 --> 00:03:27.148
<i>Yeah, you're doing all right.</i>

00:03:27.164 --> 00:03:28.782
<i>Gonna start a fire</i>

00:03:32.058 --> 00:03:33.978
You know, we could get
day jobs once in a while.

00:03:34.842 --> 00:03:35.968
Hunting's our day job,

00:03:36.484 --> 00:03:37.610
And the pay is crap.

00:03:37.857 --> 00:03:39.018
Yeah, but hustling pool,

00:03:39.754 --> 00:03:40.658
Credit-Card scams?

00:03:41.342 --> 00:03:43.013
It's not the most honest
thing in the world, Dean.

00:03:43.243 --> 00:03:44.304
Well, let's see... Honest...

00:03:45.295 --> 00:03:46.006
Fun and easy...

00:03:47.464 --> 00:03:48.379
It's no contest.

00:03:48.575 --> 00:03:48.984
Besides,

00:03:49.555 --> 00:03:50.904
We're good at it. It's
what we were raised to do.

00:03:50.973 --> 00:03:53.784
How we were raised was
jacked. Yeah, says you.

00:03:54.217 --> 00:03:55.828
We got a new gig or what? Maybe.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:58.703
Oasis Plains, Oklahoma.
Not far from here.

00:03:58.998 --> 00:04:00.356
Gas-Company employee.

00:04:01.126 --> 00:04:02.862
Dustin Burwash,

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.407
Supposedly died from creutzfeldt-Jakob.

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:06.084
Huh?

00:04:06.729 --> 00:04:08.899
Human mad cow disease. Mad cow?

00:04:10.025 --> 00:04:11.356
Wasn't that on "Oprah"?

00:04:11.902 --> 00:04:12.928
You watch "Oprah"?

00:04:16.213 --> 00:04:19.031
So this guy eats a bad burger.
Why is it our kind of thing?

00:04:20.248 --> 00:04:23.028
Mad cow disease causes
massive brain degeneration.

00:04:23.031 --> 00:04:25.498
It takes months, even years
for the damage to appear,

00:04:25.504 --> 00:04:26.688
But this guy, Dustin,

00:04:26.876 --> 00:04:29.494
Sounds like his brain
disintegrated in about an hour,

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.758
Maybe less.

00:04:30.775 --> 00:04:32.248
Okay, that's weird. Yeah.

00:04:32.717 --> 00:04:34.023
Now, it could be a disease,

00:04:34.684 --> 00:04:36.210
Or it could be something much nastier.

00:04:37.158 --> 00:04:38.801
All right, Oklahoma.

00:04:39.447 --> 00:04:40.929
Man, work, work, work.

00:04:41.839 --> 00:04:43.233
No time to spend my money.

00:04:44.362 --> 00:04:48.270
<i>We got the power, we got the glory</i>

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.520
<i>Just say you need it...</i>

00:04:58.351 --> 00:04:59.302
Travis Weaver?

00:05:01.061 --> 00:05:01.858
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:03.215 --> 00:05:05.256
Are you the Travis who
worked with uncle Dusty?

00:05:06.276 --> 00:05:07.989
Dustin never mentioned nephews.

00:05:08.552 --> 00:05:09.150
Really?

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:10.816
Well, he sure mentioned you.

00:05:10.863 --> 00:05:12.329
He said you were the greatest.

00:05:12.775 --> 00:05:13.537
Oh, he did?

00:05:14.025 --> 00:05:14.682
Huh.

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:17.181
So, we wanted to ask you...

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.917
What exactly happened out there?

00:05:20.301 --> 00:05:21.193
I'm not sure.

00:05:21.668 --> 00:05:24.366
He fell in the sinkhole. I went
to the truck to get some rope, and

00:05:24.882 --> 00:05:26.196
By the time I got back...

00:05:26.912 --> 00:05:28.120
What'd you see?

00:05:29.645 --> 00:05:30.091
Nothing.

00:05:30.813 --> 00:05:31.552
Just Dustin.

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.370
No wounds or anything?

00:05:33.816 --> 00:05:34.731
Well, he was bleeding

00:05:34.942 --> 00:05:37.346
From his eyes and his ears, his nose,

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:38.742
That's it.

00:05:39.376 --> 00:05:41.170
So do you think it could
be this whole mad cow thing?

00:05:42.866 --> 00:05:43.535
I don't know.

00:05:44.145 --> 00:05:45.353
That's what the doctors are saying.

00:05:45.423 --> 00:05:46.327
But if it was,

00:05:46.972 --> 00:05:51.324
He would have acted strange beforehand,
like dementia, loss of motor control.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.321
You ever notice anything like that? No.

00:05:53.699 --> 00:05:54.252
No way.

00:05:55.502 --> 00:05:57.816
Yeah, but if it wasn't some
disease, what the hell was it?

00:05:59.017 --> 00:05:59.895
That's a good question.

00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:00.472
Yep.

00:06:00.682 --> 00:06:02.095
Can you tell us where this happened?

00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:03.251
Yeah.

00:06:27.068 --> 00:06:27.524
Huh.

00:06:29.075 --> 00:06:29.796
What do you think?

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.502
I don't know,

00:06:31.517 --> 00:06:34.107
But if that guy Travis was right,
it happened pretty damn fast.

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:35.700
So what?

00:06:36.023 --> 00:06:37.675
Some sort of creature
chewed on his brain?

00:06:37.698 --> 00:06:39.125
No, there'd be an entry wound.

00:06:39.546 --> 00:06:41.244
Sounds like this thing
worked from the inside.

00:06:45.079 --> 00:06:45.605
Huh.

00:06:46.732 --> 00:06:48.588
It looks like there's only room for one.

00:06:49.399 --> 00:06:50.466
You want to flip a coin?

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.740
Dean, we have no idea what's down there.

00:06:55.273 --> 00:06:56.768
All right, I'll go if you're scared.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:58.051
Scared?

00:06:58.456 --> 00:06:59.568
Flip the damn coin.

00:07:03.267 --> 00:07:04.063
Call it in the air...

00:07:04.326 --> 00:07:04.905
Chicken.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:07.534
I'm going.

00:07:07.602 --> 00:07:08.511
I said I'd go.

00:07:08.824 --> 00:07:09.833
I'm going.

00:07:10.252 --> 00:07:11.100
All right.

00:07:13.009 --> 00:07:14.358
Don't drop me.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.607
So, you found some beetles

00:07:20.712 --> 00:07:22.050
In a hole in the ground.

00:07:22.929 --> 00:07:24.360
That's shocking, Sam.

00:07:24.888 --> 00:07:26.929
There were no tunnels, no tracks,

00:07:27.352 --> 00:07:29.885
No evidence of any other
kind of creature down there.

00:07:30.135 --> 00:07:31.886
You know, some beetles do eat meat.

00:07:31.905 --> 00:07:34.692
Now, it's usually dead meat, but...
How many did you find down there?

00:07:34.964 --> 00:07:35.424
10.

00:07:36.865 --> 00:07:39.230
It would take a whole lot more than
that to eat out somebody's brain.

00:07:39.343 --> 00:07:40.563
Well, maybe there were more.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.002
I don't know. It sounds
like a stretch to me.

00:07:43.024 --> 00:07:45.862
We need more information on
the area, the neighborhood,

00:07:45.886 --> 00:07:48.525
Whether something like this
has ever happened before.

00:07:50.507 --> 00:07:51.024
What?

00:07:51.739 --> 00:07:53.088
I know a good place to start.

00:07:54.654 --> 00:07:56.929
I'm kind of hungry for a
little barbecue, how about you?

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.152
What, we can't talk to the locals?

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.374
And the free food's got nothing to do
with it? Of course not. I'm a professional.

00:08:04.956 --> 00:08:05.453
Right.

00:08:25.413 --> 00:08:27.991
Growing up in a place like
this would freak me out.

00:08:28.657 --> 00:08:29.295
Why?

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.862
The manicured lawns, the"how
was your day, honey?"...

00:08:33.962 --> 00:08:35.440
I'd blow my brains out.

00:08:36.895 --> 00:08:38.713
There's nothing wrong with normal.

00:08:39.945 --> 00:08:41.880
I'd take our family over normal any day.

00:08:46.098 --> 00:08:47.940
Welcome. Is this the barbecue?

00:08:48.034 --> 00:08:50.274
Yeah, not the best weather, but...

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:54.204
I'm Larry Pike, the developer here,
and you are? Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:54.468 --> 00:08:56.063
Sam, Dean, good to meet you.

00:08:56.474 --> 00:08:59.078
So, you two are interested
in Oasis Plains? Yes, sir.

00:08:59.606 --> 00:09:00.462
Let me just say

00:09:00.568 --> 00:09:04.052
That we accept homeowners of
any race,religion, color, or...

00:09:04.622 --> 00:09:05.948
Sexual orientation.

00:09:07.578 --> 00:09:08.599
We're brothers.

00:09:09.381 --> 00:09:13.229
Our father is getting on in years, and
we're just looking for a place for him.

00:09:13.323 --> 00:09:13.909
Great,

00:09:14.097 --> 00:09:16.220
Great. Well, seniors are
welcome, too. Come on in.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:22.389
You said you were the developer?

00:09:22.588 --> 00:09:25.475
18 months ago, I was walking
this valley with my survey team.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:28.598
There was nothing here but
scrub brush and squirrels,

00:09:28.796 --> 00:09:31.414
And you know what? We built
such a nice place to live

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.107
That I actually bought into
it myself. This is our house.

00:09:34.276 --> 00:09:38.512
We're the first family in Oasis
Plains. This is my wife, Joanie.

00:09:38.588 --> 00:09:39.451
Hi, there. Hi,

00:09:39.498 --> 00:09:41.056
Nice to meet you. Sam and Dean.

00:09:41.217 --> 00:09:42.531
Sam. Joannie.

00:09:42.587 --> 00:09:44.314
Tell them how much you
love the place, honey.

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:47.641
And lie if you have to because
I need to sell some houses.

00:09:48.758 --> 00:09:50.194
Boys, if you'll excuse me.

00:09:51.048 --> 00:09:54.604
Don't let his salesman routine scare
you. This really is a great place to live.

00:09:54.746 --> 00:09:56.632
Hi, I'm Linda Bloom, head of sales.

00:09:56.726 --> 00:09:58.368
And Linda was second to move in.

00:09:58.481 --> 00:10:00.264
She's a very noisy neighbor, though.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.335
She's kidding, of course.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.216
I take it you two are interested
in becoming homeowners.

00:10:06.921 --> 00:10:08.150
Well... Y-Yeah.

00:10:08.153 --> 00:10:13.359
Well, let me just say that we accept
homeowners of any race, religion, color,or...

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.752
Sexual orientation.

00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:16.608
Hmm.

00:10:16.772 --> 00:10:17.476
Right.

00:10:17.851 --> 00:10:19.963
Uh, I'm gonna go talk to Larry.

00:10:20.291 --> 00:10:21.159
Okay, honey?

00:10:26.817 --> 00:10:28.377
You have three choices...

00:10:28.495 --> 00:10:30.547
Carpet, hardwood, and tile.

00:10:30.618 --> 00:10:31.345
Whoa,

00:10:32.014 --> 00:10:33.386
Someone likes bugs.

00:10:34.008 --> 00:10:37.023
My son. He's into insects.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.258
He's very inquisitive.

00:10:40.009 --> 00:10:40.630
Hmm.

00:10:40.783 --> 00:10:44.009
Who can say no to a steam
shower? I use mine every day.

00:10:44.419 --> 00:10:45.440
Sounds great.

00:10:45.575 --> 00:10:48.836
You also have three different
whirlpool tubs to choose from.

00:10:48.843 --> 00:10:51.022
The hardware for the tubs
include nickel, brass,

00:10:51.074 --> 00:10:54.057
And when you see the kitchens,
you can choose from... Excuse me.

00:10:54.102 --> 00:10:55.521
Um, okay.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:08.871
Is this yours?

00:11:09.194 --> 00:11:10.851
You gonna tell my dad? I don't know.

00:11:11.041 --> 00:11:11.983
Who's your dad?

00:11:12.688 --> 00:11:13.373
Yeah.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.110
Larry usually skips me in
the family introductions.

00:11:16.215 --> 00:11:19.781
Ouch. First-Name basis with the
old man... sounds pretty grim.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.752
Well, I'm not exactly brochure material.

00:11:22.072 --> 00:11:24.424
Well, hang in there. It gets
better. Alright? I promise.

00:11:24.958 --> 00:11:25.568
When?

00:11:25.591 --> 00:11:26.213
Matthew!

00:11:35.369 --> 00:11:37.715
I am so sorry about my son and his...

00:11:37.844 --> 00:11:39.334
Pet. It's no bother.

00:11:39.838 --> 00:11:40.894
Excuse us.

00:11:48.112 --> 00:11:49.285
Remind you of somebody?

00:11:54.036 --> 00:11:54.669
Dad?

00:11:56.154 --> 00:11:57.480
Dad never treated us like that.

00:11:58.266 --> 00:12:00.354
Well, dad never treated you
like that. You were perfect.

00:12:00.365 --> 00:12:01.843
He was all over my case.

00:12:03.598 --> 00:12:04.783
You don't remember?

00:12:05.662 --> 00:12:08.055
Maybe he had to raise his voice,
but sometimes you were out of line.

00:12:08.072 --> 00:12:08.794
Right.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:12.677
Right, like when I said I'd rather
play soccer than learn bow hunting.

00:12:12.871 --> 00:12:14.420
Bow hunting's an important skill.

00:12:15.557 --> 00:12:16.296
Whatever.

00:12:17.681 --> 00:12:19.417
How was your tour?

00:12:19.604 --> 00:12:21.610
It was excellent.I'm ready to buy.

00:12:21.805 --> 00:12:23.612
So you might be onto something.

00:12:24.245 --> 00:12:26.943
Looks like Dustin Burwash wasn't
the first strange death around here.

00:12:27.107 --> 00:12:27.705
What happened?

00:12:27.862 --> 00:12:29.712
About a year ago,
before they broke ground,

00:12:29.772 --> 00:12:32.011
One of Larry's surveyors
dropped dead while on the job.

00:12:32.359 --> 00:12:34.936
Get this... severe allergic
reaction to bee stings.

00:12:35.252 --> 00:12:36.484
More bugs. More bugs.

00:12:39.047 --> 00:12:41.412
I've heard of killer
bees, but killer beetles?

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.496
What is it that could
make different bugs attack?

00:12:45.261 --> 00:12:48.183
Well, hauntings sometimes
include bug manifestations.

00:12:48.218 --> 00:12:50.699
Yeah, but I didn't see any
evidence of ghost activity.

00:12:50.849 --> 00:12:51.949
Yeah, me neither.

00:12:53.747 --> 00:12:56.894
Maybe they're being controlled
somehow... by something or someone.

00:12:57.429 --> 00:12:58.672
You mean like "Willard"?

00:12:58.706 --> 00:13:00.292
Yeah, bugs instead of rats.

00:13:01.816 --> 00:13:07.344
There are cases of psychic connections between
people and animals, elementals, telepaths.

00:13:07.356 --> 00:13:09.444
Yeah, that whole Timmy/Lassie thing.

00:13:10.754 --> 00:13:12.032
Larry's kid...

00:13:12.607 --> 00:13:13.862
Bugs for pets.

00:13:14.331 --> 00:13:15.481
Matt? Yeah.

00:13:17.284 --> 00:13:20.686
He did try to scare the realtor with
a tarantula. Think he's our willard?

00:13:20.873 --> 00:13:21.788
I don't know.

00:13:21.847 --> 00:13:23.489
Anything's possible, I guess.

00:13:25.667 --> 00:13:27.555
Ooh, hey, pull over here.

00:13:36.418 --> 00:13:37.814
What are we doing here?

00:13:41.685 --> 00:13:43.268
It's too late to talk to anybody else.

00:13:45.201 --> 00:13:47.617
We're gonna squat in an empty house?

00:13:48.239 --> 00:13:50.193
I want to try the steam shower. Come on.

00:13:51.108 --> 00:13:51.976
Come on!

00:14:19.633 --> 00:14:22.940
Atoko valley county began
mandatory insecticide

00:14:22.978 --> 00:14:25.709
Spraying across a wide
swath of the district today.

00:14:25.749 --> 00:14:31.482
Authorities say the decision to spray was made
because of several recent cases of west nile virus,

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:35.989
Coupled with a dramatic increase in
the mosquito population in some areas.

00:14:36.309 --> 00:14:40.792
Although some residents cite concerns about
the high levels of pesticide being used...

00:15:06.025 --> 00:15:09.263
Aaah! Aaah!

00:15:38.831 --> 00:15:40.070
You ever coming out of there?

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.140
What?!

00:15:41.412 --> 00:15:44.387
Dean, a police call came
in on the scanner. Hold on.

00:15:44.429 --> 00:15:47.300
Someone was found dead three
blocks from here. Come on.

00:15:49.864 --> 00:15:51.338
This shower is awesome.

00:15:51.572 --> 00:15:52.448
Come on.

00:16:20.688 --> 00:16:22.828
Okay, look, I don't know
anything more right now.

00:16:22.875 --> 00:16:24.489
I'll have to call you back.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.343
All right.

00:16:26.751 --> 00:16:28.478
Hello, you're back early.

00:16:28.496 --> 00:16:32.109
Yeah, we wanted to take another look
at the neighborhood. What's going on?

00:16:34.355 --> 00:16:37.808
You guys met Linda
Bloom at the barbecue?

00:16:37.986 --> 00:16:38.822
The realtor.

00:16:39.403 --> 00:16:40.436
Well, she, uh,

00:16:41.331 --> 00:16:42.541
Passed away last night.

00:16:43.996 --> 00:16:44.690
What happened?

00:16:46.053 --> 00:16:47.339
I'm still trying to find out.

00:16:47.902 --> 00:16:49.704
I identified the body for the police.

00:16:51.233 --> 00:16:52.960
I'm sorry. This isn't a good time.

00:16:53.224 --> 00:16:53.825
It's okay.

00:16:53.984 --> 00:16:54.857
Excuse me.

00:16:58.247 --> 00:16:59.552
You know what we have to do, right?

00:17:00.696 --> 00:17:03.286
We got to get in that house.
See if we got a bug problem.

00:17:30.882 --> 00:17:32.402
This looks like the place.

00:17:46.076 --> 00:17:46.968
Spiders.

00:17:47.689 --> 00:17:48.874
From spider boy?

00:17:49.062 --> 00:17:49.812
Matt.

00:17:51.619 --> 00:17:52.405
Maybe.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.133
Isn't his house that way?

00:18:17.192 --> 00:18:18.142
Yep.

00:18:21.649 --> 00:18:23.163
So where's he going?

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:50.045
Hey, Matt.

00:18:50.855 --> 00:18:51.864
Remember me?

00:18:52.821 --> 00:18:53.794
What are you doing out here?

00:18:53.912 --> 00:18:55.284
We want to talk to you.

00:18:56.868 --> 00:18:58.416
You're not here to buy a house, are you?

00:18:59.456 --> 00:19:00.218
Wait,

00:19:01.039 --> 00:19:02.330
You're not serial killers?

00:19:02.682 --> 00:19:04.781
No, no. No, I think you're safe.

00:19:06.118 --> 00:19:07.151
So, Matt...

00:19:08.298 --> 00:19:10.139
You sure know a lot about insects.

00:19:11.265 --> 00:19:11.840
So?

00:19:13.034 --> 00:19:15.181
Did you hear what happened
to Linda, the realtor?

00:19:16.999 --> 00:19:18.371
I hear she died this morning.

00:19:18.554 --> 00:19:19.633
Mm, that's right.

00:19:19.997 --> 00:19:21.240
Spider bites.

00:19:22.108 --> 00:19:22.859
Matt,

00:19:23.727 --> 00:19:26.026
You tried to scare her with a spider.

00:19:27.653 --> 00:19:28.251
Wait,

00:19:28.943 --> 00:19:30.374
You think I had
something to do with that?

00:19:30.961 --> 00:19:32.028
You tell us.

00:19:32.826 --> 00:19:34.820
That tarantula was a joke.

00:19:35.418 --> 00:19:38.908
Anyway, that wouldn't explain the
bee attack or the gas-Company guy.

00:19:40.268 --> 00:19:41.571
You know about those?

00:19:42.005 --> 00:19:43.377
There is something going on here.

00:19:43.846 --> 00:19:44.937
I don't know what,

00:19:45.039 --> 00:19:45.520
But

00:19:45.943 --> 00:19:47.761
Something's happening with the insects.

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:49.508
Let me show you something.

00:19:57.356 --> 00:20:00.358
So, if you knew about all this
bug stuff, why not tell your dad?

00:20:00.464 --> 00:20:02.294
Maybe he could clear everybody out.

00:20:02.458 --> 00:20:04.171
Believe me, I've tried, but

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.201
Larry doesn't listen to me.

00:20:06.447 --> 00:20:07.104
Why not?

00:20:07.456 --> 00:20:08.441
Mostly?

00:20:08.582 --> 00:20:10.565
He's too disappointed in his freak son.

00:20:12.336 --> 00:20:13.251
I hear ya.

00:20:13.928 --> 00:20:14.702
You do?

00:20:17.001 --> 00:20:18.162
Matt, how old are you?

00:20:18.233 --> 00:20:19.030
16.

00:20:20.368 --> 00:20:23.124
Well, don't sweat it 'cause in two
years something great's gonna happen.

00:20:23.804 --> 00:20:25.117
What? College.

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:28.214
You'll be able to get out of
that house and away from your dad.

00:20:28.801 --> 00:20:31.302
What kind of advice is that? A
kid should stick with his family.

00:20:36.428 --> 00:20:37.461
How much further, Matt?

00:20:37.633 --> 00:20:38.641
We're close.

00:20:59.965 --> 00:21:02.171
I've been keeping track of
the insect population. It's

00:21:02.393 --> 00:21:04.153
Part of an A.P. Science class.

00:21:05.502 --> 00:21:06.769
You two are like peas in a pod.

00:21:08.831 --> 00:21:09.757
What's been happening?

00:21:09.992 --> 00:21:10.813
A lot.

00:21:11.505 --> 00:21:14.027
I mean, from bees to earthworms,

00:21:14.457 --> 00:21:15.583
Beetles...

00:21:15.712 --> 00:21:17.190
You name it. It's

00:21:17.248 --> 00:21:19.043
Like they're congregating here.

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:19.759
Why?

00:21:20.275 --> 00:21:21.201
I don't know.

00:21:23.826 --> 00:21:24.612
What's that?

00:22:01.437 --> 00:22:02.622
There's something down there.

00:22:09.308 --> 00:22:10.681
Oh, come on.

00:23:01.132 --> 00:23:03.885
So, a bunch of skeletons
in an unmarked grave.

00:23:04.002 --> 00:23:05.973
Yeah, maybe this is a haunting...

00:23:06.102 --> 00:23:07.404
Some pissed-Off spirits,

00:23:07.744 --> 00:23:10.042
Some unfinished business. Yeah, maybe.

00:23:10.124 --> 00:23:12.083
The question is, why bugs

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:13.268
And why now?

00:23:13.725 --> 00:23:15.203
That's two questions.

00:23:16.529 --> 00:23:18.148
So, with that kid back there...

00:23:18.484 --> 00:23:20.971
How could you tell him to just
ditch his family like that?

00:23:21.182 --> 00:23:22.379
Just, uh,

00:23:22.778 --> 00:23:24.443
I know what the kid's going through.

00:23:24.767 --> 00:23:28.251
How about telling him to respect his old
man? How's that for advice? Dean, come on.

00:23:28.955 --> 00:23:30.632
This isn't about his old man.

00:23:30.714 --> 00:23:32.017
You think I didn't respect dad.

00:23:32.134 --> 00:23:33.354
That's what this is about.

00:23:34.498 --> 00:23:35.964
Just forget it. Sorry I brought it up.

00:23:36.023 --> 00:23:37.055
I respected him,

00:23:37.818 --> 00:23:39.202
But no matter what I did,

00:23:39.448 --> 00:23:40.692
It was never good enough.

00:23:40.809 --> 00:23:43.472
What are you saying, that dad
was disappointed in you? Was?

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:45.653
Is...

00:23:46.123 --> 00:23:48.257
Always has been. Why
would you think that?

00:23:48.304 --> 00:23:50.040
Because I didn't want to bow hunt

00:23:50.209 --> 00:23:53.153
Or hustle pool, because I wanted
to go to school and live my life,

00:23:53.168 --> 00:23:55.552
Which in our whacked-Out
family made me the freak.

00:23:57.627 --> 00:23:59.961
Yeah, you were kind of like the
blond chick in "the munsters."

00:24:01.299 --> 00:24:01.944
Dean,

00:24:02.683 --> 00:24:05.228
You know what most dads are when
their kids score a full ride?

00:24:06.202 --> 00:24:06.917
Proud.

00:24:08.419 --> 00:24:10.612
Most dads don't toss their
kids out of the house.

00:24:11.957 --> 00:24:13.212
I remember that fight.

00:24:14.279 --> 00:24:17.036
In fact, I seem to recall a few choice
phrases coming out of your mouth.

00:24:21.839 --> 00:24:22.614
You know,

00:24:23.130 --> 00:24:25.816
Truth is, when we finally do find dad,

00:24:26.743 --> 00:24:28.772
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:24:30.555 --> 00:24:32.556
Sam, dad was never disappointed in you.

00:24:33.788 --> 00:24:34.480
Never.

00:24:35.747 --> 00:24:36.932
He was scared.

00:24:37.655 --> 00:24:38.828
What are you talking about?

00:24:38.875 --> 00:24:41.538
He was afraid of what could have
happened to you if he wasn't around.

00:24:43.063 --> 00:24:44.763
But even when you two weren't talking,

00:24:45.604 --> 00:24:47.845
He used to swing by
Stanford whenever he could,

00:24:48.607 --> 00:24:49.557
Keep an eye on you,

00:24:50.296 --> 00:24:51.587
Make sure you were safe.

00:24:52.279 --> 00:24:53.217
What?

00:24:54.633 --> 00:24:55.278
Yeah.

00:24:59.443 --> 00:25:01.085
Why didn't he tell me any of that?

00:25:03.049 --> 00:25:05.618
It's a two-Way street, dude. You
could have picked up the phone.

00:25:11.401 --> 00:25:13.236
Come on, we're gonna be
late for our appointment.

00:25:21.553 --> 00:25:23.066
So, you two are students?

00:25:23.491 --> 00:25:24.558
Yeah.

00:25:24.664 --> 00:25:26.916
Yeah, we're in your class.

00:25:27.163 --> 00:25:28.465
Anthro 101.

00:25:28.863 --> 00:25:30.025
Oh, yeah.

00:25:30.095 --> 00:25:30.869
So,

00:25:30.940 --> 00:25:32.910
What about the bones, Professor?

00:25:33.788 --> 00:25:36.545
This is quite an
interesting find you've made.

00:25:36.592 --> 00:25:40.639
I'd say they're 170
years old, give or take.

00:25:41.225 --> 00:25:43.055
The time frame and the geography

00:25:43.074 --> 00:25:44.998
Heavily suggest native american.

00:25:45.444 --> 00:25:48.781
Were there any tribes or
reservations on that land?

00:25:48.863 --> 00:25:51.561
Not according to the historical record,

00:25:51.632 --> 00:25:52.559
But

00:25:52.993 --> 00:25:54.201
The, uh...

00:25:54.248 --> 00:25:58.389
Relocation of native peoples
was quite common at that time.

00:25:58.635 --> 00:25:59.374
Right.

00:26:00.178 --> 00:26:00.812
Well,

00:26:01.328 --> 00:26:02.864
Are there any local legends,

00:26:03.076 --> 00:26:05.293
Oral histories about the area?

00:26:06.278 --> 00:26:07.463
Well...

00:26:08.073 --> 00:26:11.639
You know, there's a
euchee tribe in Sapulpa.

00:26:11.869 --> 00:26:13.628
It's about 60 miles from here.

00:26:15.036 --> 00:26:17.003
Someone out there might know the truth.

00:26:20.112 --> 00:26:21.144
All right.

00:27:07.538 --> 00:27:08.742
Joe Whitetree?

00:27:10.468 --> 00:27:13.483
We'd like to ask you a few
questions, if that's all right.

00:27:14.087 --> 00:27:15.624
We're students from the university.

00:27:15.682 --> 00:27:17.735
No, you're not. You're lying.

00:27:19.776 --> 00:27:20.574
Um,

00:27:21.172 --> 00:27:23.964
The truth is... You know
who starts sentence with

00:27:24.089 --> 00:27:25.169
"Truth is"?

00:27:25.567 --> 00:27:26.564
Liars.

00:27:31.463 --> 00:27:33.222
Have you heard of Oasis Plains?

00:27:33.269 --> 00:27:35.732
It's a housing development
near the Atoka valley.

00:27:38.448 --> 00:27:39.469
I like him.

00:27:40.161 --> 00:27:41.393
He's not a liar.

00:27:42.484 --> 00:27:43.657
I know the area.

00:27:45.041 --> 00:27:47.035
What can you tell us
about the history there?

00:27:47.172 --> 00:27:48.275
Why do you want to know?

00:27:48.944 --> 00:27:50.187
Something...

00:27:50.586 --> 00:27:51.653
Something bad

00:27:52.521 --> 00:27:54.492
Is happening in Oasis Plains.

00:27:55.459 --> 00:27:59.154
We think it might have something to do
with some old bones we found down there...

00:28:00.363 --> 00:28:01.829
Native american bones.

00:28:06.692 --> 00:28:09.003
I'll tell you what my
grandfather told me,

00:28:09.765 --> 00:28:11.607
What his grandfather told him.

00:28:12.357 --> 00:28:13.835
200 years ago,

00:28:14.102 --> 00:28:16.835
A band of my ancestors
lived in that valley.

00:28:17.586 --> 00:28:21.187
One day, the american
calvary came to relocate them.

00:28:24.270 --> 00:28:25.865
They were resistant...

00:28:26.499 --> 00:28:28.165
Calvary impatient.

00:28:29.748 --> 00:28:31.519
As my grandfather put it,

00:28:32.552 --> 00:28:33.387
On a night,

00:28:33.516 --> 00:28:34.560
The moon

00:28:34.888 --> 00:28:35.850
And the sun

00:28:36.131 --> 00:28:38.372
Shared the sky as equals,

00:28:39.662 --> 00:28:42.348
The calvary first raided our village.

00:28:42.966 --> 00:28:43.999
They murdered,

00:28:44.702 --> 00:28:45.535
Raped.

00:28:46.614 --> 00:28:48.970
The next day, the calvary came again,

00:28:49.252 --> 00:28:51.351
And the next and the next.

00:28:51.750 --> 00:28:54.847
And on the sixth night, the
calvary came one last time,

00:28:55.992 --> 00:28:58.010
And by the time the sun rose,

00:28:58.186 --> 00:29:00.320
Every man, woman, and child

00:29:00.391 --> 00:29:02.124
Still in the village

00:29:02.476 --> 00:29:03.508
Was dead.

00:29:08.125 --> 00:29:09.955
They say on the sixth night,

00:29:10.108 --> 00:29:12.712
As the chief of the village lay dying,

00:29:13.064 --> 00:29:14.940
He whispered to the heavens

00:29:15.785 --> 00:29:19.116
That no white man would
ever tarnish this land again.

00:29:20.036 --> 00:29:21.045
Nature

00:29:21.420 --> 00:29:22.605
Would rise up

00:29:23.273 --> 00:29:24.857
And protect the valley,

00:29:25.021 --> 00:29:28.106
And it would bring as many
days of misery and death

00:29:28.677 --> 00:29:29.826
To the white man

00:29:30.483 --> 00:29:32.606
As the calvary had
brought upon his people.

00:29:34.401 --> 00:29:35.492
Insects.

00:29:36.380 --> 00:29:37.799
That sounds like nature to me.

00:29:39.348 --> 00:29:40.415
Six days?

00:29:40.685 --> 00:29:42.785
And on the night of the sixth day,

00:29:43.683 --> 00:29:45.314
None would survive.

00:29:53.743 --> 00:29:55.655
When did the gas-Company man die?

00:29:56.640 --> 00:29:59.244
Let's see, we got here
tuesday, so friday the 20th.

00:29:59.765 --> 00:30:00.668
March 20th.

00:30:01.618 --> 00:30:03.049
That's the spring equinox.

00:30:03.753 --> 00:30:06.111
The night, the sun and the
moon share the sky as equals.

00:30:06.207 --> 00:30:10.042
So every year about this time,
anybody in Oasis Plains is in danger.

00:30:10.711 --> 00:30:14.296
Larry built his neighborhood on cursed land.
And on the sixth night... that's tonight.

00:30:14.625 --> 00:30:18.050
If we don't do something, Larry's
family will be dead by sunrise.

00:30:19.395 --> 00:30:20.803
So how do we break a curse?

00:30:21.131 --> 00:30:22.269
You don't break a curse.

00:30:22.668 --> 00:30:24.850
You get out of its way. We got
to get those people out now.

00:31:43.064 --> 00:31:46.079
Yes, mr. Pike, there's a main-Line
gas leak in your neighborhood.

00:31:46.161 --> 00:31:47.709
God, really? And how big?

00:31:47.815 --> 00:31:50.560
Well, it's fairly extensive.
I don't want to alarm you, but

00:31:50.689 --> 00:31:54.501
We need your family out of the vicinity for
at least 12 hours or so, just to be safe.

00:31:54.639 --> 00:31:55.648
And who is this again?

00:31:55.707 --> 00:31:58.440
Travis Weaver. I work for
Oklahoma gas and power.

00:31:58.487 --> 00:31:59.061
Uh-Huh.

00:31:59.270 --> 00:32:03.106
The problemis I know Travis. He's worked
with us for a year. So who is this?

00:32:03.634 --> 00:32:04.652
Uh...

00:32:06.342 --> 00:32:07.386
Give me the phone.

00:32:16.376 --> 00:32:17.009
Hello?

00:32:17.126 --> 00:32:18.123
Matt, it's Sam.

00:32:18.405 --> 00:32:20.407
Sam, my backyard's
crawling with cockroaches.

00:32:20.408 --> 00:32:23.856
Matt, just listen. You have to get your
family out of that house right now, okay?

00:32:24.148 --> 00:32:25.002
What, why?

00:32:25.890 --> 00:32:27.139
Because something's coming.

00:32:27.796 --> 00:32:28.632
More bugs.

00:32:28.980 --> 00:32:30.238
Yeah, a lot more.

00:32:31.328 --> 00:32:33.422
My dad doesn't listen in
the best of circumstances.

00:32:33.442 --> 00:32:36.389
What am I supposed to tell him?
You got to make him listen, okay?

00:32:36.588 --> 00:32:37.821
Give me the phone. Give me the phone!

00:32:38.032 --> 00:32:41.179
Matt, under no circumstances are you to
tell the truth. He'll just think you're nuts.

00:32:41.308 --> 00:32:43.832
But he's my... Tell him you have
a sharp pain in your right side,

00:32:43.891 --> 00:32:45.452
And you got to go to the hospital, okay?

00:32:45.583 --> 00:32:47.274
Yeah. Yeah, okay.

00:32:51.125 --> 00:32:52.158
"Make him listen."

00:32:52.862 --> 00:32:53.954
What are you thinking?

00:33:05.995 --> 00:33:07.626
Damn it, they're still here. Come on.

00:33:15.457 --> 00:33:17.637
Get off my property
before I call the cops!

00:33:17.684 --> 00:33:19.363
Mr. Pike, listen. Dad,

00:33:19.868 --> 00:33:20.889
They're just trying to help.

00:33:20.936 --> 00:33:21.993
Get in the house!

00:33:22.544 --> 00:33:24.212
Sorry. I told him the truth.

00:33:24.270 --> 00:33:26.102
We had a plan, Matt.
What happened to the plan?

00:33:26.912 --> 00:33:28.520
Look, it's twelve a.M.

00:33:28.661 --> 00:33:30.058
They are coming any minute now.

00:33:30.117 --> 00:33:33.204
You need to get your family
and go before it's too late.

00:33:33.335 --> 00:33:35.330
Oh, yeah, you mean
before the biblical swarm.

00:33:35.506 --> 00:33:37.937
What do you think really
happened to that realtor, huh?

00:33:38.078 --> 00:33:39.475
And the gas-Company guy?

00:33:39.921 --> 00:33:41.740
You don't think something
weird's going on around here?

00:33:41.860 --> 00:33:44.173
Look, I don't know who
you are, but you're crazy.

00:33:44.186 --> 00:33:46.646
You come near my boy or my family again,

00:33:46.743 --> 00:33:47.818
We're gonna have a problem.

00:33:47.863 --> 00:33:50.537
Well, I hate to be a downer, but we got
a problem right now. Dad, they're right.

00:33:50.756 --> 00:33:51.688
We're in danger.

00:33:52.650 --> 00:33:54.663
Matt, get inside now!

00:33:55.039 --> 00:33:56.083
Why won't you listen to me?!

00:33:56.173 --> 00:33:58.543
Because this is crazy!
It doesn't make any sense!

00:33:58.866 --> 00:33:59.400
Look,

00:33:59.660 --> 00:34:01.268
This land is cursed.

00:34:01.606 --> 00:34:05.010
People have died here. Are you gonna
really take that risk with your family?

00:34:05.022 --> 00:34:05.533
Wait.

00:34:07.712 --> 00:34:08.426
You hear it?

00:34:12.846 --> 00:34:13.905
What the hell?

00:34:18.511 --> 00:34:20.577
It's time to go. Larry, get your wife.

00:34:21.298 --> 00:34:21.719
Guys.

00:34:25.947 --> 00:34:27.036
Oh, my god.

00:34:29.116 --> 00:34:30.326
We'll never make it.

00:34:30.378 --> 00:34:32.354
Everybody in the house.
Everybody in the house!

00:34:32.570 --> 00:34:33.239
Let's go!

00:34:38.178 --> 00:34:40.358
Is there anyone else in the
neighborhood? No, it's just us.

00:34:40.997 --> 00:34:42.199
Honey, what's happening?

00:34:42.759 --> 00:34:43.803
What's that noise?

00:34:44.968 --> 00:34:45.937
Call 911.

00:34:46.756 --> 00:34:47.633
Joanie!

00:34:47.889 --> 00:34:48.520
Okay.

00:34:49.775 --> 00:34:51.370
I need towels.

00:34:51.482 --> 00:34:54.742
We got to lock this place up. Come on, doors,
windows, the fireplace, everything. Okay?

00:34:55.441 --> 00:34:56.454
Phones are dead.

00:34:56.535 --> 00:34:57.893
They must have chewed
through the phone lines.

00:35:04.063 --> 00:35:05.097
And the power lines.

00:35:05.338 --> 00:35:06.191
Maybe my cell.

00:35:09.504 --> 00:35:10.446
No signal.

00:35:11.013 --> 00:35:11.987
You won't get one.

00:35:12.720 --> 00:35:14.380
They're blanketing the house.

00:35:31.397 --> 00:35:32.455
So, what do we do now?

00:35:33.182 --> 00:35:34.173
We try to outlast it.

00:35:36.211 --> 00:35:38.969
Hopefully the curse will
end at sunrise. Hopefully?

00:36:01.985 --> 00:36:03.770
Bug spray? Trust me.

00:36:06.729 --> 00:36:07.276
What is that?

00:36:17.781 --> 00:36:18.661
The flue.

00:36:21.475 --> 00:36:23.248
I think everybody needs to get upstairs.

00:36:34.468 --> 00:36:36.726
Everybody upstairs now! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:36:40.107 --> 00:36:41.456
Quick!

00:36:50.263 --> 00:36:52.748
Okay, Joanie, go, go, go.

00:36:52.785 --> 00:36:53.736
Matt, go.

00:36:55.297 --> 00:36:56.388
Hurry!

00:37:03.166 --> 00:37:04.152
You in? Yeah.

00:37:07.312 --> 00:37:09.074
Come on!

00:37:15.685 --> 00:37:17.082
My god, what's that?!

00:37:23.415 --> 00:37:24.661
Something's eating through the wood.

00:37:26.087 --> 00:37:26.928
Termites.

00:37:31.370 --> 00:37:32.759
All right, everybody get back.

00:37:32.914 --> 00:37:34.356
Get back! Get back!

00:37:34.386 --> 00:37:34.956
Get back!

00:37:36.030 --> 00:37:36.818
Matt.

00:38:38.599 --> 00:38:40.992
Huddle together. Cover your faces.

00:38:51.752 --> 00:38:52.515
Look!

00:39:53.882 --> 00:39:54.828
What, no goodbye?

00:39:55.353 --> 00:39:56.194
Good timing.

00:39:56.307 --> 00:39:57.778
Another hour and we'd have been gone.

00:39:58.334 --> 00:39:58.949
For good?

00:39:59.888 --> 00:40:00.498
Yeah.

00:40:00.551 --> 00:40:04.320
The development's been put on hold while the
government investigates those bones you found,

00:40:04.755 --> 00:40:06.144
But I'm gonna make damn sure

00:40:06.274 --> 00:40:07.408
No one lives here again.

00:40:08.204 --> 00:40:09.652
You don't seem too upset about it.

00:40:10.885 --> 00:40:14.121
Well, this has been the biggest
financial disaster of my career, but,

00:40:15.547 --> 00:40:16.658
Somehow...

00:40:18.559 --> 00:40:19.866
I really don't care.

00:40:35.151 --> 00:40:36.060
What's this?

00:40:36.292 --> 00:40:37.118
I don't know.

00:40:38.327 --> 00:40:39.010
They

00:40:39.288 --> 00:40:40.609
Kind of weird me out now.

00:40:43.190 --> 00:40:44.590
Yeah, I should hope so.

00:41:05.616 --> 00:41:06.697
I want to find dad.

00:41:08.504 --> 00:41:09.307
Yeah, me too.

00:41:10.921 --> 00:41:12.025
Yeah, but I just...

00:41:15.415 --> 00:41:16.841
I want to apologize to him.

00:41:20.384 --> 00:41:21.008
For what?

00:41:23.582 --> 00:41:25.293
All the things I said to him.

00:41:28.151 --> 00:41:29.615
He was just doing the best he could.

00:41:32.983 --> 00:41:34.590
Well, don't worry, we'll find him,

00:41:35.798 --> 00:41:37.252
And you'll apologize,

00:41:38.073 --> 00:41:40.696
And within five minutes, you guys
will beat each other's throats.

00:41:44.774 --> 00:41:46.616
Yeah, probably.

00:41:49.372 --> 00:41:50.944
Let's hit the road. Let's.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.500
